 "text": "9/29/26, 9:39 AM\nUse\n\nMove-in and move-out processing have the following enhancements:\n\ne ECSBTIOI1 (IS-U move-in: determine application form)\n\nThis enhancement enables you to specify a default value for the application form used for the welcome letter.\n\ne ECSBTIO2 (IS-U move-in: determine budget billing amount)\n\nThis enhancement enables you to specify a default value for the budget billing amount.\n\ne ECSBTIO4 (IS-U move-in: determine transfer contract)\n\nThis enhancement enables you to specify a default value for the transfer contract.\n\ne EMDKOOOI!1 (IS-U utility contract: include subscreens and check fields)\n\nThis enhancement enables you to enter default values in contract fields. When you create a move-in, information about the\ninstallations that have to be allocated to the contract is transferred. The enhancement is run during every PBO (process before\noutput) on the move-in screen.\n\ne EC500001 (IS-U move-in: determine security deposit amount and reason)\n\nThis enhancement enables you to specify a default value for the amount of, and reason for a cash security deposit. It is run during\nevery PBO (process before output) on the move-in screen.\n\ne ECSBTOO1 (IS-U: move-out - determine default values for Customizing of table TE490A)\n\nThis enhancement is used, for example, to assign default data to the application form for the move-out confirmation.\n\ne ECSBTIO3 (IS-U move-in: user-defined checks)\n\nThis enhancement is used for checking field values on the move-in screen.\n\ne ECSBTOO2 (IS-U move-out: user-defined checks)\n\nThis enhancement is used for checking field values on the move-out screen.\n\ne ECSBTMRI (Indicator used to allocate default values to the Create service notification/order functions)\n\nFor more information, see Service Notifications and Orders.\n\ne ECSBTOO1 (IS-U: move-in/move-out \u2014 customer-specific messages in the information log (environment log)\n\nThis enhancement is used to add user-define messages in the environment log.\n\nEnhancements for the Screen Layout\n\nYou can include standard and user-defined fields for the contract account and business partner in direct maintenance. To do this,\nuse the following enhancements:\n",
